## Install

```sh
go get {{project_slug}}
```

## Use

```go
d, err := libname.Parse("1d12h") // 36h0m0s
if errors.Is(err, libname.ErrSyntax) {
	// not a duration
}
fmt.Println(libname.Format(d)) // 1d12h
```

The package documentation and runnable examples are on pkg.go.dev, or run `make doc`.

## Compatibility

The module follows semantic versioning. [docs/public-api.md](docs/public-api.md) lists the exported API and what counts as a breaking change; `make api-check` enforces it against the last release.

## Development

Requires Go, make, a C compiler (for the race detector) and [golangci-lint](https://golangci-lint.run/).

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make test` | Unit tests, examples and fuzz seeds with the race detector |
| `make fuzz` | Fuzz each target for FUZZTIME (10s by default) |
| `make consumer` | Use the library from a separate module, as a dependent would |
| `make api-check` | Fail on an incompatible change to the exported API |
| `make lint` | golangci-lint, including doc comments on every exported name |
| `make ci` | Everything CI runs |

See [docs/DEVELOPMENT.md](docs/DEVELOPMENT.md) and [docs/releasing.md](docs/releasing.md).

